;; L8 -- the evidence-cache filename tag said v3 while the content said
;; :reflection-rule {:version 2}. checks/library_graph_lint.clj:121 held the
;; literal "futon3-spider-evidence-occurrences-v3-" and passed rule-version only
;; into the sha, so the number a reader sees in the name was fixed at 3 from
;; cad5034 onward while the rule behind the hits moved 2 -> 3 at 299f47b.
;;
;; The tag is now computed from rule-version and read-index-cache refuses a
;; file whose tag and recorded version disagree. That refusal would have
;; orphaned the caches the corpus pins resolve to, so the eight files whose
;; content states :version 2 were RENAMED to the name the fixed function
;; computes for them, not regenerated: regenerating would need a fresh walk of
;; the live store, which produces a different :basis and so would not be the
;; index those attestations were judged against.
;;
;; The sha changes because one line changed inside each file as well as the
;; name: the header's own :cache-path string. checks/spider_fleet.clj:161 reads
;; (or (:cache-path cache) (recompute)) and hands that path to every worker, so
;; a renamed file carrying its old name would have sent the fleet to a path that
;; no longer exists. Nothing else in any file was touched.

{:item :L8
 :at "2026-09-02"
 :by "claude-cli"
 :fix "checks/library_graph_lint.clj evidence-cache-path / cache-version-failure / read-index-cache"
 :not-renamed
